@startuml SequenceDiagram_Premium_Payment_Part1_Client
' Part 1: Client - Subscription screen and checkout
!theme plain
title Premium and Payment - Part 1: Client (Flutter)

skinparam maxMessageSize 100

actor User
participant "GoRouter" as Router
participant "SubscriptionScreen" as Screen
participant "SubscriptionRepository" as SubRepo
participant "PaymentSuccessScreen" as SuccessScreen

== Open Premium ==
User -> Router : Tap Premium or /subscription
Router -> Screen : SubscriptionScreen
Screen -> Screen : ref.watch(plans), ref.watch(currentSubscription)
Screen -> SubRepo : getPlans(), getCurrentSubscription()
SubRepo --> Screen : plans, currentSub
Screen -> User : Current plan card (if active), plan list, Subscribe

== Refresh (pull to refresh) ==
User -> Screen : Pull to refresh
Screen -> SubRepo : invalidate providers, getCurrentSubscription()
SubRepo --> Screen : fresh data

== Subscribe ==
User -> Screen : Tap Subscribe on plan
Screen -> Screen : show loading dialog
Screen -> SubRepo : subscribe(plan.id)
SubRepo -> SubRepo : POST /subscribe, get checkoutUrl
SubRepo -> SubRepo : launchUrl(checkoutUrl, externalApplication)
SubRepo --> Screen : true or false
Screen -> User : close dialog, SnackBar "Redirecting..." or "Failed to start checkout"
User -> User : Browser opens Stripe Checkout (external)

== Success return ==
User -> Router : Deep link or web redirect to /payment/success
Router -> SuccessScreen : PaymentSuccessScreen
SuccessScreen -> SuccessScreen : addPostFrameCallback invalidate providers
SuccessScreen -> User : "Payment Successful!", Back to Home button
User -> SuccessScreen : Tap Back to Home
SuccessScreen -> Router : context.go(/home)

== Cancel return ==
User -> Router : Redirect to /payment/cancel
Router -> Screen : SubscriptionScreen (same as open)

@enduml
